2026-11-03T04:55:39.7331243Z   "scope": "Existing cleanup owner and actual files/service, explicit HTML loading through the existing bounded loader/service, PNG header bounds through existing metadata/attachment/file consumers, and BR-v1 shared byte bounds with opened-file admission, finite fault controls, actual service/Box/image/channel consumers and fresh retry. FUA-v1 retains local URL authority/conversion, pure admission and native path/byte/service controls; its counter measures reader-boundary entries, not OS syscalls, and contacts no live share. Synthetic allocation faults do not prove real process-wide OOM recovery. LFA-v1 native admission selects the shared converter, metadata facade and actual Channel/web-media consumers plus whole AgentManagement preflight. The separate Linux App receipt executes actual private Runner/AgentManagement sinks and Session custody; this native receipt does not prove that execution. HTML policy and stale-snapshot controls do not establish generated origin, a durable marker or database pruning. No public Gateway registration, complete read-capability/root identity, cancellation, hostile Windows open deadline, native 32-bit, frontend/Runner/full MIME or image codec, packaged or whole-media acceptance.",
